{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "First Day of Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": " New Ways Ahead"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.  "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "probation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a period of time after an employee starts while he or she is supervised closely"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At least, that's true while we are under probation. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you talk about work in publishing."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "factual"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pertaining to facts or real information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We think we will be proofreading texts and check for the accuracy of factual information for books or specialized magazines."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "illustrator"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " an artist who creates illustrations, drawings or other images for a publication"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When illustrations are needed, I expect we will be researching for images, or making arrangements with photographers or illustrators."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "expenditure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "costs; things you need to spend money on"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've learned to organize the steps and calculate expenditures of a project in the courses I took."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "project management"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "organizing the work of different people contributing to a large project"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Then there's the aspect of project management. That seems interesting, too. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le06ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect Tense with Past Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense with past tenses for two reasons:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. to talk about states or events that started in the past and continue to now. You can refer to these events with the words since or ever since.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">She'<span class=\"strong\">s been</span> better behaved <span class=\"underline\">since she had</span> that warning.<br/> <span class=\"underline\">Ever since I met you</span>, I'<span class=\"strong\">ve felt</span> so much better about things.</span><br/><br/>  2. to describe repeated or long-term feelings or thoughts about past events<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">ve often wondered</span> why they <span class=\"underline\">decided</span> to promote Rhonda.<br/> I'<span class=\"strong\">ve always felt</span> we did the right when we <span class=\"underline\">hired</span> her</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Ever since we met Ms. Moore, I've had the same impression."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Mr. Brody has also been very interested in my ideas for new books and articles every time to spoke to him."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've learned to organize the steps and calculate expenditures of a project in the courses I took."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use a variety of tenses to talk about the future. Let's compare the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " Look at the chart for an outline of the meanings/uses and the form of the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future Continuous - 1\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk about an event or action in progress <span class=\\\"underline\\\">at some time</span> in the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We will be proofreading texts and check for the accuracy of factual information for books or specialized magazines.  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future Continuous - 2\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk about an event or action in progress <span class=\\\"underline\\\">during a period</span> in the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I think we will be doing more editing and revision work than original writing.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk about an event that <span class=\\\"underline\\\">will be finished</span> before a specified time in the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">By the end of the day, we will have met almost everybody by the end of the day.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I hope we will be learning more about how to deal with copyright issues."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When illustrations are needed, we will be researching for images, or making arrangements with photographers or illustrators."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "You are a manager. You need to explain the role of new employee. Write a dialogue of 12 - 15 lines."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Future Continuous tense (for example: You will be researching \u2026)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The new employee asks questions related to his or her work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Answer the employee's questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice your dialogue with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I explain a new employee's role using the Future Continuous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask questions related to work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I answer questions related to work."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le06ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le06ob09re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le06ob09re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Ouff! We've made it to lunchtime!<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: We've received a lot of information since we started this morning! By the end of the day, we will have met almost everybody in the office.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Yeah, tell me about it. The company seems very well organized.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Absolutely. Can we go over our new responsibilities? Ms. Moore talked about that briefly.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I think we will be doing more editing and revision work than original writing. At least, that's true while we are under probation.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I think you're right. Ever since we met Ms. Moore, I've had the same impression.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le06ob09re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: We think we will be proofreading texts while we check for the accuracy of factual information.   As soon as illustrations are needed, I expect we will be researching for images, or making arrangements with photographers or illustrators.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Then there's the aspect of project management. That seems interesting, too. I've learned to organize the steps and calculate expenditures of a project in the courses I took. They said we would be liaising with authors, marketing staff, designers and printers at each stage of the process. I hope we will be learning more about how to deal with copyright issues, like\nresearching titles to make sure they have not been used already.", "id": 2, "time": "32000", "image": "engenn10le06ob09re2img08.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Ms. Moore mentioned something about commissioning articles and recruiting authors. Have you been listening to everything she said?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Not really. We'll have to ask.  I hope we will be given the chance to propose some of our original writing.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Mr. Brody has also been very interested in my ideas for new books and articles every time to spoke to him. I have a lot of ideas to share as soon as we have settled in to our new roles.", "id": 3, "time": "70900", "image": "engenn10le06ob09re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can request or report about facts about events or actions in the workplace."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss hopes and expectations for the future in job related topics."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about my work responsibilities. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are your responsibilities at work?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are the responsibilities of other people you work with?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Would you like to have more responsibilities? Why or why not?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " Are you ready for your new responsibilities?"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nAdam and Kristi talk about their morning at BFP Publishing. The company seems <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">well-organized</span>!\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attemp